)", "Infectious monocytosis with constitutional symptoms (less likely with 35% blasts instead of monocytes)", "Myeloproliferative neoplasm with leukostasis (considered but subsumed under hematologic aetiology phrase)"], "alarm_features": ["Fever", "Unintentional weight loss", "Night sweats", "Leukocytosis with blasts"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.004, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Leukostasis is more characteristic of blast crisis in chronic myeloid disorders (like CML-BC) than de novo AML. This weakly favors CML-BC (B3.1) and weakly arg…"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.06238098298861689, "posterior": 0.05142589048922704, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["The presence of 35% blasts in peripheral blood with leukocytosis and constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss) provides moderate support for myeloid neoplas…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 0.85, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.6496442849155103, "posterior": 0.48025964448273795, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["The presence of 35% blasts in peripheral blood with leukocytosis and constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss) provides moderate support for myeloid neoplas…"], "unres