f blast crisis in chronic myeloid disorders (like CML-BC) than de novo AML. This weakly favors CML-BC (B3.1) and weakly argues against myeloid malignancy (B1) as the primary category."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of chronic phase features (e.g., splenomegaly, basophilia) in the physical exam argue against CML-BC (B3.1) as the primary diagnosis?", "summary": "Lack of splenomegaly and basophilia reduces support for CML-BC (B3.1), but does not definitively exclude it given variable clinical presentation in blast crisis."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of elevated hemoglobin (normal hemoglobin) in labs argue against polycythemia vera in accelerated phase (B3.2) as the primary diagnosis?", "summary": "Normal hemoglobin levels weaken PV-AP (B3.2), which typically presents with elevated hemoglobin in chronic phase."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of bone marrow fibrosis or splenomegaly in the physical exam argue against primary myelofibrosis in accelerated phase (B3.3) as the primary diagnosis?", "summary": "Lack of fibrosis and splenomegaly in physical exam weakly argues against PMF-AP (B3.3), which commonly presents with splenomegaly and marrow fibrosis in accelerated phase."}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": true, "reason": "Leukostasis from blast crisis (35% blasts in peripheral blood with leukocytosis 57,500/mm³) causing neurological symptoms (headache, blurry vision, ataxia) is a time-critical condition requiring immediate intervention.", "required_actions": ["Initiate leukapheresis", "Administer IV fluids for hydration and renal support"]}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "[static mode override] Active emergency interrupt for leukostasis (35% blasts + leukocytosis causing neurological symptoms) requires immediate leukapheresis and hydration. Further diagnostic expansion would delay critical intervention. — emergency_override suppressed in static_diagnosis_qa mode"}, "turn_budget_used": 2, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.8, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.2907179471180324, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'elevated white blood cell count', 'elevated red blood cell count', 'Leukocytosis', 'Myelofibrosis'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "root_revision_needed": false, "program_faults": [], "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B3", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.65}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B3.1", "label": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Blast Crisis (CML-BC)", "posterior": 0.291, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 2, "disconfirming": 1, "last_disconfirming_digest": "Lack of splenomegaly and basophilia reduces support for CML-BC (B3.1), but does not definitively exclude it given varia…"}, "action_intents": [{"t": 1, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B3.2", "B3.3", "B2"]}}
